    "body": "Scripted interactive-tutorial experiment: a tutor overlay types demos into a dedicated scratch slide, locks the editor during the tutor's turn, and gates progress on predicates over the user's zipper (e.g. \"text contains `* 4`\", \"has a probe\").\n\nTO FIX (introduced by the 2026-07-31 dev merge): checkpoint restore now round-trips through printed text (`Printer.of_zipper` -> string `Paste`, since dev's `Action.Paste` went string-only). That resets probe/projector models, drops pins and backpack contents, and churns all ids. The adventure model already stores the checkpoint as a structured `Zipper.t` \u2014 restore should swap in a fresh `CellEditor.Model` (the way `ScratchMode.ResetCurrent` and undo restore state) instead of pasting. Related pre-existing bug: checkpoint capture runs before same-batch scheduled agent actions apply, so `probes_intro`'s second checkpoint captures a probe the narrative just removed.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
